<article class="env-remark" id="49EA73">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/49EA73">Remark <span data-tag="49EA73">8.3.2.10</span>.</a> Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a functor between $\mathbf{S}$-enriched categories which satisfies condition $(i)$ of Definition <a href="/tag/F14D54" data-tag="F14D54">8.3.2.9</a>. Let $X \in \calC $ and $Y \in \calC '$ be objects. If $\calC '$ is locally fibrant, then every morphism $[f]: F(X) \rightarrow Y$ in $\rm {h} \it {\calC '}$ can be represented by an equivalence $f: F(X) \rightarrow Y$ in $\calC '$. Let $\overline{Y}$ be an object of $\calC $ such that $F( \overline{Y} = Y$. Since $\mathbf{1}_{\mathbf{S}}$ is a cofibrant object of $\mathbf{S}$ and the map $\bHom _{\calC }( X, \overline{Y} ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }( F(X), Y)$ is a fibration, Proposition <a href="/tag/F03C0F" data-tag="F03C0F">8.2.3.1</a> implies that $[f]$ can be lifted to an isomorphism $[\overline{f}]: X \rightarrow \overline{Y}$ in $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ if and only if $f$ can be lifted to an equivalence $\overline{f}: X \rightarrow \overline{Y}$ in $\calC $. Consequently, when $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ is locally fibrant, condition $(ii)$ is equivalent to the following analogous assertion: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii')$"><p>
For every equivalence $f: F(X) \rightarrow Y$ in $\calC '$, there exists an equivalence $\overline{f}: X \rightarrow \overline{Y}$ in $\calC $ such that $F( \overline{f} ) = f$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
